# BP Authoring Planner Policy

This policy defines how UnrealMCP should classify a user request before
authoring Blueprint assets or graph nodes.

## Status Priority

1. `blocked_until_reinforced`
2. `requires_review`
3. `safe_to_author`

If one request contains both safe and blocked work, the blocked status wins. The
safe part may be split into a smaller request only after the blocked part is
removed or explicitly deferred.

## Safe Now

- Blueprint shell or simple Actor/Component Blueprint creation.
- Existing component composition and exposed property/default setup.
- Ordinary reflected function calls and simple graph flow.
- Blueprint Event Dispatcher declaration, call, bind, assign, unbind, and clear
  lifecycle nodes.
- Enhanced Input graph glue against existing input assets.
- Sample/temp Animation Blueprint creation from a Skeleton or SkeletalMesh
  through `create_anim_blueprint_sample`.
- Sample/temp Animation Blueprint regular state-machine authoring through
  `ensure_anim_state_machine_sample_variant`.
- Read-only animation metadata inspection through
  `inspect_animation_asset_metadata_guarded`.
- Runtime-only animation state, state-machine response, BlendSpace, bone/socket,
  and selected-node probe evidence through the dedicated AnimBP probe commands.
- SkeletalMeshComponent mesh and AnimBP default assignment through
  `set_skeletal_mesh_component_anim_defaults`.
- Sample/temp Post Process, Modify Bone, Trail Controller, and RigidBody helper
  routes when they stay inside the documented sample scopes.

## Requires Review

- Latent function calls and continuation ordering.
- UMG widget-specific event binding.
- Broad "convert this C++" requests that have not been split into safe graph
  glue versus native behavior.
- Original, durable, saved, overwrite, replace, delete, or production AnimBP
  mutation. The automatic safe route is sample/temp first.
- ControlRig requests. ControlRig has a separate learning and authoring route
  and should not be silently classified as generic AnimBP auto-authoring.

## Blocked Until Reinforced

- Native or arbitrary delegate lifecycle authoring.
- Generic delegate requests that are not explicitly Blueprint Event Dispatcher
  lifecycle work.
- Async action proxy callback exec pins and cancellation/cleanup topology.
- Gameplay Ability System internals, AbilityTasks, and prediction flow.
- Replication, RPC, ReplicationGraph, authority policy, and networking state.
- CommonUI tree/layer/activation policy.
- Advanced AnimBP graph/state-machine rewrites not covered by current dedicated
  commands, including conduits, state aliases, nested machines, custom
  transition graphs, arbitrary rule graphs, Linked Anim Graph, Linked Anim
  Layer, Sub Anim Instance, and arbitrary AnimGraph insert-before/after or
  replacement edits.
- Custom K2 nodes and editor graph expansion behavior.
- GameFeature or Experience architecture.
- Slate/editor-only C++ behavior.

## Validation Rule

Every safe authoring plan must include compile validation and graph re-read
steps. Unknown requests default to `requires_review`, not `safe_to_author`.
AnimBP safe plans must use the dedicated AnimBP MCP commands, keep writes under
`/Game/_MCP_Temp` or `/Game/_MCP_Sample` by default, and must not persist
UnrealMCP/MCP-only references into generated results.
